' plan-114-E: a `STATE T` clause on a record field is gated exactly as it is on a
' binding (spec 15.5) -- `T` must be a copyable, defaultable DATA type. A
' resource is none of those, so `STATE fs::File` is refused.
'
' THIS FIXTURE PINS A GAP THAT WAS REAL. The binding check lives behind an
' `explicit_type` gate in ir/verify/ops.rs and never saw a field, so when
' plan-114-D opened the grammar a field could declare a resource as its own state
' payload and NOTHING rejected it -- all the way to codegen -- while a binding
' with the identical clause had always been refused. Measured before the fix:
' `mfb build -ast -ir` emitted no diagnostic at all.
'
' So this is not "verify the existing rule still applies". The rule had to be
' routed to the field position, and this is what says it stays routed.
IMPORT fs
IMPORT io

TYPE Holder
  handle AS RES fs::File STATE fs::File
END TYPE

FUNC main AS Integer
  io::print("unreachable")
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
